   "evidence": "HEAD constructs the baseline using `await executeRun(f.deps, run.id, ...)` and compares `expect(statuses).toEqual(baseline)`. RunContext resolves `deps.checkpointer ?? localCheckpointer(deps.store)`, while recordingCheckpointer also wraps `localCheckpointer(store)`. Consequently, both sides share adapter defects. The separate unit test checks notification counts for status patches but never exercises the title patch used by this mutation. At base, triage calls `ctx.store.updateRun(...)` directly; at head, the actual adapter correctly delegates through `writeRun: (runId, patch, state) => store.updateRun(runId, patch, state)`. This is a missing independent test oracle, not an observed production notification defect."
